# Project rules — N32

- **Active programme:** `N32` — ≤60M non-embedding params, **32,768-token context**, trained end to end on one RTX 4060 in <72 h. Spec: `docs/pipeline/README.md`.
- **Read first, always:** `docs/pipeline/P19-agent-operating-protocol.md`, then `docs/ASSESSMENT-2026-07-30.md`.
- **Find your task:** `ls docs/pipeline/results/` — the highest-numbered file is the last completed stage; the next stage is the job. One stage at a time.
- **Wave protocol is RETIRED.** Never create a wave, letter-named phase, forever pack, or new numbering scheme.
- **Deleted history:** waves W–BH, EvoGen C++, and the old harness were removed in the 2026-07-30 reset. They live only in the git tag `legacy/waves-w-bh`. **Do not restore or read them** — 341,926 lines of the protocol that failed.

## Seven laws

| # | Law |
|---|---|
| R1 | Held-out **bits-per-byte** is primary. Never report perplexity. |
| R2 | No claim without a committed artifact (git hash · config hash · seed · wall time). Markdown is never evidence. |
| R3 | Retrieval and generation measured separately, always. |
| R4 | Embedding vs non-embedding params reported separately, always. |
| R5 | A stage that costs no FLOPs is not research. |
| R6 | One pipeline. No waves. |
| R7 | A failed gate stops the pipeline. Fix the cause, never the gate. |

## Hard prohibitions

- Serving any answer from a lookup table.
- Weakening a gate so a stage passes.
- Leaving a hypothesis in `HOLD` / `DEFER` — resolve to `PROMOTE` or `FALSIFY`.
- Adding an npm script no stage references.
- Writing a summary document instead of running an experiment.

**Three failed attempts at a gate → stop and ask the user.**

- Research tracks: `docs/pipeline/P13-quantum-inspired-training-lab.md` (quantum-inspired; classical controls mandatory) · `docs/hypotheses/README.md` (100-architecture catalogue, fixed size).
- Caps: cyclomatic ≤10 per function; `npm run verify` before every commit.
- Repository hygiene (what never enters git): `docs/REPO-HYGIENE.md`.
